# Code Standard and Best Practices

Our goal is to evolve the codebase towards a more modular, maintainable, and professional development practices.

1. Separation of Concerns (SoC)
    - Each module, component, or service should have a single, well-defined responsibility.
    - clarity and ensures adherence to the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP), which is fundamental to creating maintainable code.
    
2. Organize utilities into more granular, domain-specific files 




